		{
			x: 6.196428571428569d
			y: -0.875d
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Why So Slow?"
			description: [
				"&dSo why don't we just take all items, tag em, and dump them back all at once?"
				""
				"&5Visibility."
				""
				"&dSee, we have to treat the Audubon Worm like an actual, mutating virus. But from the 'bad' end of it, I guess."
				""
				"&5Like that one game you showed me, sis. Level up the virus slowly. It can't kill fast or it just burns out or gets cured super fast before it can spread enough."
				""
				"&dRight. If we hit them with a big attack, they'll quickly see it and neutralize it. You saw how fast they countered me removing Item Level requirements, yeah? Same thing."
				""
				"&5This is one reason why we are putting a price on things in our Shop. Infecting more things but at a slower, steady pace. Sure, you could dump thousands of Cobblestone at once, but that stuff is cheap, so they wouldn't notice."
			]
			dependencies: [
				"14E05D152CF5C051"
				"65766106B865F4F9"
			]
			size: 0.75d
			id: "7DE302BB0723FB8A"
			tasks: [{
				id: "14508C0895B7123A"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Slow and Steady"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Rune Power"
			x: 9.0d
			y: 2.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&dWell that's interesting. Looks like they changed how the whole Rune thing worked."
				""
				"&5Really? Well, Runes are components you need not only to make some items, like Wands, but also power them, like ammunition."
				""
				"&dAnyways, Bandit, each rune is of a different 'element'. Not just wind, fire, earth..."
				""
				"&5But also Wither, Lunar, Poison, etc. Many you cannot use until you level up your Runation skill."
				""
				"&dUsed to be, you had to find a Rune Shrine on each world to make a rune. Or get lucky with a Rune Bag lottery or something."
				""
				"&5Now you can just craft them. You should start with the Wind Rune."
			]
			dependencies: ["14E05D152CF5C051"]
			id: "7543E03FC25521E7"
			tasks: [
